  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH THURSDAY/...\nIssued at 215 AM CDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\nThanks to consensus among ensemble clusters and deterministic \nguidance, confidence is high in a benign and uneventful pattern \nthrough the upcoming workweek. Continuous troughing over the West \nCoast and ridging to our east-southeast will keep upper-level flow \nweakly southwesterly through this portion of the period. This \nsupports warm air advection, though subtly given the weakness of the \nflow. As a result, daily temperatures will only gradually warm \nthrough the workweek. Values closer to seasonal normals are at least \nexpected through the first half of the workweek, but how much warmer \nwe climb toward the end of the week is uncertain. The NBM \npushes afternoon highs to around 80 degrees Thursday and Friday,\nthough that is roughly 5 degrees warmer than the 75th \npercentile of ensemble guidance. This is due to the bias-\ncorrected guidance composing the NBM, and this guidance is \nseveral degrees warmer than their non-biased counterparts. Given\nthe bias factor applied here may be too warm given our seasonal\ncooling, confidence is low in the NBM's late-week temperature \nforecast. \n\nGiven the weakness of the flow aloft and lack of any notable \ndisturbances in deterministic guidance, confidence is high in dry \nconditions prevailing through this portion of the period. This is \nsupported by nearly all ensemble members showing this stretch being \nrain-free.",
